  "guideBasicsTitle": "How to play",
  "guideBasicsBody": "Each question has four options (sometimes True / False) and a timer. Tap an option before time runs out.\n• Both sides see the same question at the same moment; network delay is compensated on the server.\n• A wrong answer or a timeout costs nothing, it just scores 0.\n• If you answer wrong, the right answer is not shown during the match; after the match you can see every question and answer on the result screen.\n• Questions you saw in the last 30 days are not asked again.\n• If your connection drops, the app rejoins the match by itself. Staying away too long or dropping too often loses the match.",
  "guideScoringTitle": "Scoring",
  "guideScoringBody": "A right answer earns points in three parts:\n• Base points: 80–120 depending on the question's difficulty.\n• Speed bonus: the sooner you answer, the more, up to +100. Answering at the last moment gives 0.\n• Streak bonus: +20 for 3–4 right in a row, +40 from 5.\nOne question is worth at most 260 points. True / False questions are worth half (at most 150).\nAt the end the higher total wins; on a tie, right answers and speed decide.",
  "guideTypesTitle": "Match types",
  "guideTypesBody": "• Quick Duel: 7 questions, 15 s each. A short, relaxed match.\n• Ranked: 10 questions, 15 s, multiple choice only. Played only through matchmaking; the only mode that changes your Season Points (SP).\n• Sudden Death: 10 s per question. When one side is right and the other wrong in a round, the match ends. Difficulty rises every 3 rounds; if nothing is decided after 30 rounds, the higher score wins.\n• Marathon: 25 questions, 12 s each, with a 15 s break after question 12.",
  "guideCategoryTitle": "Topic modes",
  "guideCategoryBody": "Outside Ranked you can choose how questions are picked:\n• Standard: questions come mixed from different topics.\n• Blind Challenge: a question's topic stays hidden until it is answered.\n• Category Master: every question comes from one topic you choose. In matchmaking you only meet players looking for the same topic.\n• Mixed Battle: 3 topics are set for the match; each round the sides take turns picking one of them (10 s).\n• Revenge: the losing side may ask for a revenge within 24 hours after the match; half of the questions come from a topic they choose. A series has at most 3 revenge matches.",
  "guideTeamsTitle": "Teams and couples",
  "guideTeamsBody": "Besides one-on-one you can play 2v2, 3v3, 4v4 and Couple formats. You can create a team and invite friends, or become a couple with a friend. Team matches have three answer modes:\n• Shared Answer: the team proposes an option together and one member locks it in. You get 5 extra seconds to agree.\n• Individual Turns: the next player in the rotation answers each question.\n• Fast Team Round: everyone answers alone; the team's points are the average of its members.\nA team scores on the same scale as a single player; a bigger side does not earn extra points.",
  "guideDailyTitle": "Daily Challenge",
  "guideDailyBody": "Every day everyone answers the same 10 questions in the same order. The day resets at midnight Istanbul time.\n• You have one official attempt a day; later runs are practice and don't affect the board.\n• The board ranks by right answers first, then by total answer time.\n• Right answers are not shown during the day. You can see them the next day in \"Yesterday's answers\".\n• If your connection drops, you can continue within 2 minutes; the clock keeps running meanwhile.\n• The official run earns XP (30 + 5 per right answer) and keeps your play streak.",
  "guideRoomsTitle": "Private rooms and challenges",
  "guideRoomsBody": "• Private room: create a room and share its code with friends. The host picks the match type, format and topic mode; the match starts when everyone is ready. After the match everyone returns to the room.\n• Challenge: send a match invite straight to a friend from your friends list.\n• These matches earn XP but no SP or leaderboard points, so friends can't farm points against each other.",
  "guideTournamentsTitle": "Tournaments",
  "guideTournamentsBody": "Tournaments are knockout brackets. Register, then check in during the last hour before the start; players who don't check in are left out.\n• Each round you get a notice when your match is ready; if you don't join in time you lose by walkover.\n• There are solo, team and couple tournaments.\n• Rewards: 1st 300 XP, 2nd 150 XP, 3rd 75 XP, everyone else 20 XP.",
  "guideLabTitle": "Question Lab",
  "guideLabBody": "Make your own quiz: start with one question and grow it to up to 30 with \"Add question\". You choose the answer time (10, 15 or 20 s).\n• Draft quizzes can only be played with friends in a private room and give no rewards.\n• Send a quiz for review; once approved it is published, anyone can discover and play it, and players earn XP.\n• You earn no XP from your own quiz.",
  "guideLeaguesTitle": "Leagues, seasons and SP",
  "guideLeaguesBody": "Season Points (SP) come only from Ranked: win +30, draw +10, loss −15. From your 3rd ranked win in a row a streak bonus of +5, +10 and at most +15 is added.\n• Leagues: Bronze (0), Silver (300), Gold (800), Platinum (1600) and Diamond (2800 SP). Every league except Diamond has three divisions (III, II, I).\n• You can't drop out of a league during a season; divisions inside it can go up and down.\n• A season lasts 8 weeks. At the end you get a badge for the highest league you reached, then everyone starts again in Bronze III.",
  "guideXpTitle": "XP, levels, streaks and quests",
  "guideXpBody": "• Every completed match earns XP: 20 + 5 per right answer + a result bonus (win 15, draw 8).\n• Each level needs a little more XP than the one before; the top level is 100. Level only shows your progress and never affects matchmaking or scoring.\n• Streak: complete at least one match or an official Daily Challenge every day to grow your streak; missing a day resets it.\n• Quests: 3 daily and 3 weekly quests. Claim the reward when you finish one; you can swap one quest a day for free.\n• Badges: earn badges for wins, accuracy, speed, streaks, topics and seasons.",
  "guideBoardsTitle": "Leaderboards",
  "guideBoardsBody": "There are daily, weekly, monthly and all-time boards, each for the world, your country and your friends. Teams and couples have their own boards too.\n• Leaderboard points come only from matchmade games: win 20, draw 10, +2 per right answer.\n• The season board is ranked by SP, and the Daily Challenge has its own board.\n• Tap a player to add them as a friend or view their profile. If you make your profile private, only your friends see your stats.",
  "guideFairTitle": "Fair play",
  "guideFairBody": "• Points and results are computed only on the server; changing the app cannot change a result.\n• Right answers are hidden during a match from players who answered wrong, and in the Daily Challenge from everyone until the day is over.\n• Matches between friends give no SP or leaderboard points.\n• If a question looks wrong, use \"Report question\" after the match. Breaking the rules can lead to sanctions.",
